# `docs/ownership-seam.md` carries a generated inventory of the scaffolded tree, so
# every branch that touches an app rewrites the same counts and every rebase collided
# there (issue #866). Unsetting `merge` tells git not to attempt a content merge: the
# base's version is left in the working tree, marked conflicted, with no markers to
# unpick. The resolution is then always the same one command, and CONTRIBUTING.md
# spells it out: re-run `pnpm qcms:sync-templates`, then `git add`.
#
# Unset rather than a `merge=ours` driver, deliberately. A named driver has to be
# defined in `.git/config` in every clone and every worktree, so it is silently absent
# for whoever did not run the setup step, and a merge rule that works for some clones
# is worse than none. This attribute needs no local configuration at all.
docs/ownership-seam.md -merge
